Peter King Mike Florio talking about  some of the things that we either didn't  get to during KFC live or that we would  like to talk about some more and we  spent some time talking about Peters  interview with Bengals coach Zack Taylor  they drafted Joe Borough first overall  last Thursday night and look Peter a  year ago Joe burrow was a guy who had  spent a season at LSU had a 57%  completion percentage was pissed off  about it went back to the lab to improve  his mechanics specifically his footwork  getting his feet set when he was off  platform his completion percentage  skyrockets to north of 76 his yards  nearly doubled his touchdowns go from 16  to 60 his team goes 15 and OH  he wins the Heisman Trophy and he  becomes the no-brainer number one  overall pick in the draft so now the  challenge is getting him ready to be the  quarterback for the Cincinnati Bengals  when we consider this crazy upside down  environment we're still inhabited and  there's going to be no offseason program  by all appearances who knows when  training camp is gonna open what kind of  a challenge of the Bengals really faced  with here to get Joe borough ready to be  there week one starter well the crazy  thing one of the things I wondered with  Zack Taylor is you your quarterback who  and and who knows maybe Andy Dalton  stays and takes the first snap of the  year but for all intents and purposes  your starting quarterback going forward  might not even meet AJ green until  mid-august I mean what sort of problem  is that and you know what it reminds me  of a little bit Mike it reminds me of  those stories that you hear about  Russell Wilson like and and quite  honestly Joe burrow going to Auburn you  know in the middle of the summer and  then doing enough in summer camp to win  the starting job or like Russell Wilson  you know 19 days after he lands in  Madison Wisconsin he's named one of the  captains of the team and he gets the  starting quarterback job and he has a  great year that is what it's going to  take this year for Joe burrow to be  really good but compounding the problem  is the Zach Taylor mentioned to me look  he's going to get all the stuff mentally  when we go over it  on these teleconference things when he  has like quarterback meetings and and  all that so he'll mentally he'll know it  but you've got to do it you got to go  out and throw Andy any sand and look I  know because I asked the dad you know  Jimmy Borough Ohio University isn't open  and Athens high school isn't open those  are the two big football places where  the borough's live in Southeast Ohio and  so he's gonna have to find a field  somewhere in the area just an open field  to throw to people and he's gonna have  to find people to throw to maybe old  Athens High teammates but there's so  much about this that's gonna be a 34:31  day I can't even imagine and you know  you say he may not meet AJ green until  August I continue to be very very  curious as to how all quarterbacks and  their receivers tight ends running backs  what kind of arrangements they will make  especially before the world opens up  again because I already suspect that  some of that stuff's going on and people  are just being discreet as opposed to  what they were being a few weeks ago  when they were posting evidence of it on  social media but if you're Joe burrow  and you want to take charge of that team  you're gonna want to get together with  AJ green you want to get together with  with John Ross you're gonna want to get  together with tee Higgins you're gonna  want to get together with Joe Mixon and  really start working on getting yourself  ready to play and it's that that  mentality at Chris Sims shares from time  to time on pft live football players  just don't care maybe they should but  they don't they're not worried about the  corona virus they're confident that if  they get it they'll be fine they're not  thinking about all the potential  implications of passing it around their  families they are young they are  invincible they are strong and they are  going to do what they have to do to be  ready to go play football period so you  know there's the stuff we know about  Peter but I also think there's gonna be  the stuff that that we don't know about  and if the seasoned pros like Tom Brady  may be doing it  Joe burrow is gonna find a way to do it  too  probably so and look I think as we've  talked about before you know Tom Brady's  gonna find a way to get Mike Evans and  and Cameron braid and Chris Godwin up to  his place up in Montana and he's gonna  throw to him at some point and and I  would expect that the Bengals are gonna  try to do that with burrow and these  guys somewhere but at the very least  Mike they're gonna have to wait a little  while I think because of local  ordinances and you can't be together but  this is this is all such such a mystery  right now and that's one of the things I  was saying to somebody the other day  look I've now been a sports writer for  40 years and one month okay this by far  is the most intriguing time and the most  interesting time that I've ever been a  sports writer and III wake up every day  and think about nine things that hey I  should look into this I should look into  that so we just don't know what's gonna  happen but part of that is so intriguing  if we don't know what's gonna happen  that's what kind of makes it interesting  yeah there's been a formula every year  and I've been doing this 20 years now  every April is the same every May is the  same every June is the same it's  different names it's different twists  but it's always that same cookie cutter  on the NFL calendar and now that we've  gotten through the draft which was the  focal point for weeks the cookie cutters  are thrown out the window we have no  idea how this is gonna play out we have  no idea which teams are going to master  this new reality which teams are going  to be kicked to the curb and we can just  at this point only hope that we will see  football at some point this year and  look uh uh it's it's amazing when you  listen to some of the folks in the media  who just want to want to fire darts set  at the sports writers and the  broadcasters who are trying to be  realistic and suggest that we're being  pessimistic no we're being realistic  we're being objective we're looking at  this situation and recognizing it's  going to be different for everybody and  there is a chance there isn't going to  be football this year  as part of the the coverage that we have  to devote to this so we hopefully will  see Joe burrow with the Bengals Peter we  hopefully will see all these players on  the field but I think it's ridiculously  naive at this point to assume it will  happen without complication without  delay without the possibility that it's  just not going to happen at all I agree  and the one other point I think you  really have to consider in all of this  is and it's look it's with it's with  every rookie every rookie is going to  have a different process this year then  a normal rookie would have to me it's  one of the reasons one general manager  told me Saturday night when I said hey  how's it going and he goes you know  we're really really happy with the  intelligence of the guys who we picked  and I said explain that and he goes we  don't have any idea what these guys are  gonna go through before the season  starts so it doesn't it stand to reason  why we want people who are really smart  so that the indoctrination period both  mentally and then on the field is gonna  be a short one and you know you don't  want to be taking a lot of time if you  only have three weeks of practice before  your first game teaching all the  remedial stuff to a guy who has to play  for you and so that I think is gonna  show I think some of the best rookie  years we'll see this year we'll look  back Mike in January or February and  we'll say oh my god Kol commit was great  for the Chicago Bears because he picked  up stuff seamlessly and he adapted  quickly and that's what's Joe burrow has  to adapt quickly and seamlessly you know  for the Bengals to have a chance this  year yeah and it's all to be determined  and there's no formula there's nothing  we can look at there's no statistic  based on their past play that we can  really say aha here's the evidence  especially since burrow struggled his  first year at LSU if he had made that  transition from Ohio State to LSU and  had the year he had last year right out  of the gates then you've got evidence of  it but with a lot of these guys we just  don't know and we won't know but we can  hope and that's what we'll do and  continue to provide you with all the  information you need about what's  happening in the NFL on PFC live on PFT  ot and all of the various NBC sports  platforms thanks as always for some of  your time and we'll see you back here  again on Thursday  hi I'm Mike Tirico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from NBC  Sports
 

